 files['00-READ-ME.txt']=`${m.projectName}\n${m.revision} | ${id}\nDESIGN REVIEW AND QUOTING PACKAGE\nNOT RELEASED FOR FABRICATION\n\nThese files describe the CURRENT configurator state. All files in a handoff must have the same design ID. Save layout.json to preserve it. Inches govern, except named mm/ft/sqft columns. Numeric precision is not field accuracy. Dimensions derive from architectural PDF A-102 plus proposed casework.\n\n01 cabinets: finished case envelopes, materials, interior/shelf, front and installation intent. Base assembly includes the separate toe-height allowance; case height excludes it. Case depth excludes fronts.\n02 fronts: finished front sizes derived from reveals, drawer splits and handing, shared with the 3D model. Not CNC/cut-part dimensions.\n03 panels: installed panels/fillers, island back/ends and fridge enclosure, including scribe obligations.\n04 hardware: drawer pairs, hinges, pulls and waste kit. TBD values are deliberate, never zero quantities. Drawer machining and box sizes await actual runner SKU.\n05 toe kicks; 06 appliance envelopes; 07 countertop union zones; 08 boundary edges; 09 backsplash/waterfalls; 10 cutouts and services; 11 open decisions; 12 quantity summary.\n\nCountertop zones are contiguous layout regions, not promised single-piece fabrication blanks. Internal cabinet divisions are not stone seams. Sink cutout area is shown separately and not deducted from stone procurement area. Slab count, waste, seam locations, vein matching, support and transport/access remain fabricator work. Tile allowance is an estimate only. Waterfalls remain inside the top footprint and reduce cabinet run capacity.\n\nFinish samples, hardware, appliance manuals, sink templates, field measurements and signed shop drawings are required before manufacture. Exact stock lists, joinery/CNC files, boring diagrams, fixings and installation details must come from the maker's approved construction system. Use 11-review-decisions.csv as the handoff checklist.\n\nSource references\nWolf: ${WOLF_SOURCE}\nBlum: ${BLUM_SOURCE}\nNKBA planning recommendations: ${NKBA_SOURCE}\nCounter support coordination: ${STONE_SOURCE}\n`;
